hey guys this is vadim with max tech and  i am extremely excited  because we just got a ton of apple  silicon mac leaks  that were just revealed including the  redesigned imac  totally redesigned macbook pros two new  mac pro desktops and a new  apple display all of this just broke and  i'm more excited than ever  especially for the new redesigned  macbook pros which have been rumored for  about a year now  so in this video i'm gonna go through  all of those leaks  and give my personal thoughts and  opinions on how exactly this is gonna  play out  on these new macs and when we should  expect them to get released  so let me first start with the macbook  pros before we move on  to the others late last night ming chu  quo released a report  confirming that apple is working on two  new macs  a 14 inch and 16 inch macbook pro but  here's the best part these new macbook  pros will feature a new  flat edge design similar to the current  iphones  and ipad pro getting rid of those curved  edges  that we currently have on the macbooks  now you might be asking  why would apple do this wouldn't it make  them look very thick  well i figured out two very important  reasons why  and i'll get to them in just a minute  moving on it seems like apple is  recently doing  everything they can to satisfy the  requests of  their macbook user fan base ming chi quo  says that apple is finally getting rid  of the touch bar  instead returning to physical function  keys  this is huge because i know of so many  people that have been complaining about  the touch bar  and on my own personal 2018 15-inch  macbook pro  i've actually set the touch bar to  simply display the classic function keys  because they're so much easier to use  now some might come to the conclusion  that apple could be finally packing  in a touch screen display since they're  ditching the touch bar  and while there is a chance that that  could happen  i personally disagree here's why a long  time ago  steve jobs said touchscreen macs don't  make sense  because they're ergonomically terrible  and then in 2014  craig federighi said apple has no plans  to add a touchscreen  to a mac later phil schiller said that  it makes sense for the mac to have a  precise pointer  for user input and then once again in  2016  he said that they tried it out and  absolutely came away with the belief  that it isn't the right thing to do in  2018  craig again said that touchscreen max  would be pretty fatiguing on the  arms and even joni ive said that a touch  screen on a mac  isn't particularly useful and then just  three months ago  craig federighi was heard saying apple  wasn't even remotely  considering adding a touch screen to the  mac even with the new bixer update so  with all of that coming  directly from apple i personally doubt  that we'll be seeing a touchscreen mac  for a long time even with apple finally  ditching  the touch bar which i'm glad they're  doing because the function keys are just  better and as we already know these new  macbook pros will be coming with apple's  new  mini led displays which will basically  look  almost as good as oled displays but  without all the drawbacks  now here's another bombshell from ming  there will be  no intel cpu options for these macbook  pros going forward  in fact i personally believe that every  single mac that's about to get  redesigned  will not get an intel cpu so  new design means apple silicon chip and  as most of you already know  i think the m1x chip will be going into  both the 14 inch and  16 inch macbook pro and the performance  is gonna be insane and to confirm my  speculation  on that ming chuko also said that both  of these macbook pro models  will be using the same heat pipe design  currently used by the 16-inch macbook  pro allowing for  increased computing power which  basically means that the 14-inch  is also getting the crazy powerful m1x  chip  getting even more interesting ming said  that they're also coming  with more types of ports which i wasn't  expecting at all  this shows that apple is truly starting  to listen to their customers  and if you're wondering which ports  they're gonna have  i think that apple has a wide variety of  options because they're going to  redesign  the body itself making it flat on the  bottom  and the sides the actual sides will have  more room  for larger ports so they can potentially  add  one or two regular usb a ports if they  really wanted to  but i myself personally think that these  new macbook pros  will come with four thunderbolt 4 ports  one sd card slot a headphone jack and  one usb a port just not to make it too  busy  but i guess we'll see now the absolute  bombshell leak  is the rumor that apple is finally  bringing back the max safe  charging connector and i have a really  crazy theory  about apple's future plans for maxsafe i  believe that the main reason why apple  is giving the future macbooks  a flat side design is specifically  for the magsave feature i personally  speculate that the new flat side design  will allow apple to make a brand new  magsafe connector  that looks extremely similar to the  smart connector  on the current ipad pro so i think  there's literally going to be  three flush mounted circles or squares  on the side of the macbook pro right  next to the other ports  apple will include a new mac safe  charging cable in the box  and it simply holds on magnetically  while charging  and apple could even allow data to  travel through it now you might ask  why well you may have heard that apple  is planning to make the iphone  completely portless my theory is that  apple will literally  replace the lightning port with the same  new max safe connector right on the  bottom of the iphone as well as the mac  so the future iphone will technically be  portless  using the new completely sealed magsafe  connector  and you're going to be getting a one  meter long magsafe cable  in the box and the users who do want to  use wireless charging  can buy the maxsafe wireless charging  puck for 40  on apple's website and on the macbook  side of things you'll be getting a 2  meter long magsafe cable in the box for  charging which frees up  one of the thunderbolt ports and there  you go  apple has successfully replaced  lightning  with a new standard connector without  switching to usbc  this means that apple can continue  charging licensing fees  for this new proprietary connector and  they can continue to sell  mfi accessories just like they did with  lightning  so that's my theory and if it comes true  remember this video and by the way mark  german from bloomberg  agrees with a lot of these rumors that  mingshuko said  including the mac safe part now digging  a bit deeper into the new design  i personally believe that these macbook  pros will become  thinner to help the new flat design not  look  as thick this is exactly what apple did  with the iphone 12 lineup they had to  make it thinner  because the new flat side design makes  it look  thicker now the reason apple is going to  be able to do this with the new macbook  pros  is because they're going to pack very  cool and efficient  apple silicon chips and with those chips  will come  a brand new redesigned logic board  that's going to be taking up  much less space the touch bar is going  away  so that takes up less space and the  battery can now become  thinner and more spread out amongst the  larger interior  which comes thanks to the flat design so  yes apple will most likely  make it thinner without sacrificing  battery life because of apple silicon  and on top of that because of the new  flat design  the display portion where the webcam is  currently housed  is gonna get thicker allowing for a  1080p  webcam or maybe even face id  now as far as the release date ming chu  quo believes that they'll be coming  in the third quarter of this year which  basically puts it in between  july and the end of september so i'm  gonna personally put my money  on apple announcing these macbook pros  at wwc  in june which they've done in the past  with an official launch date  the first week of july and now let's  finally get into those other leaked macs  starting with the imac there's gonna be  two imacs  also with a new redesign which will come  with a completely flat back  and flat sides basically the same that  apple is doing to the new macbook pro  now what's very interesting is that ming  believes that the chin  will finally be going away so it's going  to look essentially like the pro display  xdr  except i think that it's probably gonna  have a small apple logo on the front  these new imacs will of course come with  the new apple silicon chips  and i personally think that the smaller  23 to 24 inch model  will come with the m1x chip just like  the new macbook pros  but the larger model will come with a  better chip  potentially with up to 20 cpu cores  and i also think that this model is  going to come with a dedicated  custom apple gpu chip now in terms of  the size  i think the larger model will come with  a new display ranging anywhere from 28  to 30 inches most likely sticking to the  same 5k resolution  but it's gonna finally come with decent  hdr support  and as far as the release date i  personally don't think they're gonna  come until  after the m1x macbook pros are released  so i'm gonna bet on sometime maybe this  fall  or maybe even winter this year now apple  is also rumored to be releasing a new  lower priced external display and i  personally think it's gonna come with  the same exact  display panel that's gonna be in the new  large imac  just like they did with the previous lg  ultra fine  4k and 5k displays so there might even  be a new 23 to 24 inch display  and a new 28 to 30 inch display and now  finally  this brings us to our last major leak of  the day  and that's rumors for mark german of  apple working on  two new mac pro desktops with one of  them coming  with a new design reminiscent of the  power mac  g4 cube this leak finally gives us a  good idea on how apple will handle  giving the mac pro the apple silicon  chip the larger mac pro that we  currently have  will simply be updated with new pci  express 4.0 support on the motherboard  new intel xeon chips new amd big navi  graphics cards  and it's going to maintain the ability  to use massive amounts of ram  and other full-size pci express cards  and i believe that this will be the  very last intel mac that will ever get  released  and i think it's going to come  potentially maybe this year the end of  december  or it's gonna come alongside the apple  silicon mac pro  next year and i think that's probably  more likely  and that redesign mac pro is gonna come  with a brand new apple silicon chip  potentially packing up to a 32 or  64 core cpu on top of that i believe  that apple will be creating  custom apple gpu cards having up to 128  cores  on one card that you can put into the  new mac pro  however it will not support third-party  graphics cards  it will only support smaller pci express  cards  like audio and networking cards but not  graphics  it'll likely pack just one large fan  that cools the entire system  and i personally think it's gonna get  released in december  of 2022 with a starting price of around  three to four thousand dollars so there  you guys have it that  was the massive arsenal of mac leaks  that we just got within the past 24  hours  so if you disagree with any of my  speculations  comment down below and click the circle  above to subscribe for more videos like  this one  and definitely check out my video on the  imac redesigned right over there  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next one

